.TH scalpel3-ctl "1" "" "The scalpel3 Controller" "The scalpel3 Controller"

.SH NAME
scalpel3-ctl \- Control and monitor a running scalpel3 instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scalpel3-ctl
[\fB-b\fR]
[\fB-c\fR]
[\fB-h\fR]
[\fB-k\fR \fIUUID\fR]
[\fB-kq\fR]
[\fB-o\fR \fIscalpel_output_dir\fR]
[\fB-p\fR]
[\fB-s\fR]
[\fB-x\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBscalpel3-ctl\fR interacts with a running \fBscalpel3\fR instance on the local machine via Unix domain sockets. It provides a "human in the loop" interface that supports initiating checkpoints, getting progress reports, terminating specific carving jobs, and controlled shutdowns.
.PP
Exactly one command option (excluding \fB-o\fR) must be specified per invocation.

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
The following options are available:

.TP
.B -b
Retrieve and display a copy of the current primary blockmap.

.TP
.B -c
Request that scalpel3 create a progress checkpoint, which updates the
INPROGRESS directories. UUIDs of files associated with reassembly jobs can
then be scrutinized and used with other options such as \fB-k\fR.
This command is available only during fragmented recovery; requests during
other phases are rejected immediately. A successful response is sent only
after the INPROGRESS update is complete.


.TP
.B -h
Say HELLO to the scalpel3 instance. Useful for verifying IPC connectivity.

.TP
.BI -k " UUID"
Kill a specific carving job, either active or queued, using its \fIUUID\fR. Use \fB-p\fR or \fB-c\fR to obtain UUIDs of candidates currently being considered.

.TP
.B -kq
List all UUIDs currently in the kill queue.

.TP
.BI -o " scalpel_output_dir"
Specify the output directory of the targeted scalpel3 instance. This is required if the target instance is not using the default "scalpel-output" directory, as the IPC endpoint (\fI.scalpel3IPC\fR) is stored there.

.TP
.B -p
List UUIDs, file types, and current lengths for all carving candidates that are either actively being reassembled or queued for reassembly.

.TP
.B -s
Display current carving statistics.

.TP
.B -x
Request that scalpel3 stop as soon as possible. If restartable checkpoint state exists, scalpel3 writes a checkpoint before exiting. If no restartable checkpoint state exists, scalpel3 exits cleanly without writing checkpoint state.

.SH EXIT STATUS
\fBscalpel3-ctl\fR exits with status 0 only after the requested operation
receives a complete response. It exits with a nonzero status for invalid
arguments, connection or transmission failures, malformed responses, or when
the scalpel3 instance closes the IPC connection before completing the response.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1)

